    "q-60009": {
      "dom_id": "step-q60009",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "The following table shows the number of cakes and cookies sold on a charity day.\n\n| Cakes | Cookies |\n| --- | --- |\n| $23$ | $121$ |\n\nRounding to the nearest ten, find the ratio of the number of cakes sold to the number of cookies sold.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's approximate the number of cakes and cookies sold by rounding to the nearest $10$:\n\n- number of cakes sold: $23⟶20$\n\n- number of cookies sold: $121⟶120$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of cakes sold to the number of cookies sold is approximately:\n\n$$\n\\frac{20}{120}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $10$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{20÷10}{120÷10}=\\frac{2}{12}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2÷2}{12÷2}=\\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of cakes sold to the number of cookies sold is approximately $\\frac{1}{6}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
