    "q-92858": {
      "dom_id": "step-q92858",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "The following table shows the weight, in kilograms, of sand and crushed stone in a concrete mix.\n\n| Sand | Crushed stone |\n| --- | --- |\n| $1\\,224$ | $1\\,645$ |\n\nRounding to the nearest hundred, determine the approximate ratio of the weight of sand to the weight of the crushed stone.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's approximate the weight of sand and crushed stone by rounding to the nearest $100$:\n\n- sand: $1\\,224⟶1\\,200$\n\n- crushed stone: $1\\,645⟶1\\,600$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the weight of sand to the weight of the crushed stone is approximately:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1\\,200}{1\\,600}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $100$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1\\,200÷100}{1\\,600÷100}=\\frac{12}{16}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $4$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{12÷4}{16÷4}=\\frac{3}{4}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the weight of sand to the weight of the crushed stone is approximately $\\frac{3}{4}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
