    "q-59992": {
      "dom_id": "step-q59992",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "The following table shows the weight, in grams, of wheat flour and sugar in a cake mix.\n\n| Wheat Flour | Sugar |\n| --- | --- |\n| $615$ | $408$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest hundred, determine the approximate ratio of the weight of wheat flour to the weight of the mix of wheat flour and sugar.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's approximate the weight of wheat flour and sugar by rounding to the nearest $100$:\n\n- Wheat flour: $615⟶600$\n\n- Sugar: $408⟶400$\n\nThus, the weight of the mix of these two ingredients is approximately $600+400=1\\,000.$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the weight of the wheat flour to the weight of the mix is approximately:\n\n$$\n\\frac{600}{1\\,000}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $100$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{600÷100}{1\\,000÷100}=\\frac{6}{10}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6÷2}{10÷2}=\\frac{3}{5}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the weight of the wheat flour to the weight of the mix of wheat flour and sugar is approximately $\\frac{3}{5}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
