      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Sam and Justin get paid for mowing neighborhood lawns. The ratio of Sam's reward to Justin's reward is $2:3.$ \nDuring a particular week, Sam received $$416.$ By rounding Sam's earnings to the nearest hundred, approximate the amount of money that Justin received.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's approximate the amount of money that Sam received:\n\n$$\n$416⟶$400\n$$\n\nThe ratio of Sam's earnings to Justin's earnings is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe numerator represents Sam's earnings  and the denominator represents Justin's earnings.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $400$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by \n $200$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 200}{3\\times 200}=\\frac{400}{600}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, Justin received approximately $$600.$",
