    "q-60058": {
      "dom_id": "step-q60058",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Marcus has two water tanks. Tank A has a capacity of $1\\,508$ liters. The ratio of the capacity of tank A to the capacity of tank B is $3:4.$ By rounding the capacity of tank A to the nearest hundred, approximate the capacity of tank B.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's approximate the capacity of tank A:\n\n$$\n1\\,508⟶1\\,500\n$$\n\nThe ratio of the capacity of tank A to the capacity of tank B is\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe numerator represents the capacity of tank A and the denominator represents the capacity of tank B.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $1,500$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by \n $500$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 500}{4\\times 500}=\\frac{1\\,500}{2\\,000}\n$$\n\nTherefore, tank B has a capacity of approximately $2\\,000$ liters.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
